      "canvasUri": "canvases/canvas-IY29lOwv--",
      "content": "Drawn from [https://www.math4wisdom.com/wiki/KnowledgeEngineering/ActiveInferenceOfAbsoluteTruth](https://www.math4wisdom.com/wiki/KnowledgeEngineering/ActiveInferenceOfAbsoluteTruth)\n\n[https://www.templeton.org/grants/grant-database](https://www.templeton.org/grants/grant-database)\n\n---\n\n# 8-13-2024 — OFI submitted!!!! 🎉🎉🎉🎉🎉🎉🎉🎉\n\nWe should hear back by October 11, 2024. \n\n\n\nTempleton Grant 2024 question\n\n## Notes\n\n**Topics**\n\n[Books by Sir John Templeton](https://archive.org/search?query=creator%3A\"Templeton%2C+John%2C+1912-2008\")\n\n- [Worldwide Laws of Life. 200 Eternal Spiritual Principles.](https://archive.org/details/worldwidelawsofl0000temp)\n\n- [The Essential Worldwide Laws of Life.](https://archive.org/details/essentialworldwi0000temp)\n\n- Active Inference as framework for exploring epistemological/ontological variations\n\n  - E.g. multiagent setting with over-/under-fitting agents, multiple realities (??) \n\n    - With multiple realities/agents — if they are fully partitioned/isolated, they are embedded and isolated in some unified thing. Or to the extent that they do interact, they are in some single unified thing. Reality is truth. \n\n    - Is there a universal relationship with such a reality? \n\n      - [https://coda.io/d/_d0SvdI3KSto/_suptXYov](https://coda.io/d/_d0SvdI3KSto/_suptXYov) ? Can we use [https://coda.io/d/_d0SvdI3KSto/_suli3zvK](https://coda.io/d/_d0SvdI3KSto/_suli3zvK) and other methods to explore possibilities for cognitive interfaces with reality and truth.  \n\n- Low/High Road — What is the bottom-up/top-down situation, who deemed this? \n\n- Innocence. → Overfitting of Experience is dogmatism. Absolute Truth — Everyone has a window/perspective/view on Absolute Truth that can be developed and expressed (e.g. with non-linear questions like What is your deepest value?). \n\n- Active Inference:\n\n  - Gives two-fold between Experience (M1) and Questions/Uncertainty (M2), opening up the possibility of understanding the relationship (M3).\n\n\n\nCommunity organizing\n\n- Inverted pyramid. \n\n  - People\n\n    - Leader is full-time supported. \n\n    - Equivalent amount split across 5 people (e.g. $5,000/year)\n\n      - Maybe doing some training. \n\n    - Equivalent amount split across 25 people ($1,000/year)\n\n      - Take what you are working \n\n  - Other Institute activities & workshops \n\n  - Overhead = +10%\n\n  - \n\nApplication instructions — \n\n- On August 13th we will:\n\n  - Review any comments on the answers. \n\n  - Review ready-for-submission state, make any last edits or side-notes. \n\n  - Daniel: Log in the application portal, ensure we are all ready to make the transfer. \n\n- August 13th after meeting, or 14th probably — D will upload to the application portal.  ",
